'===========================================================================
'Version:10   14 March 2018 Jason Ritter (JCR), Campbell Scientific
'Updated program to version 10, adding the following Public variables
'Midnt_air_temp_C - midnight 15 minute temperature at level 0
'Midnt_RH - midnight relative humidity reading
'Midnt_snow_in - midnight 15 minute snow depth

'Updated program to version 8, adding the following Public variables
'PrecipToday - Precipitation since midnight, updated every 15 minutes
'MaxGustToday - Maximum wind gust since midnight (speed at level 1 only), updated
'every 15 minutes
'WindChill_C - Wind chill at level 1 only, deg C, updated every 15 minutes,
'calculated with:
' WindChill = 35.74 + (0.6215*temp0) - (35.75*speed1^0.16) + (0.4275*temp0*speed1^0.16)
' with speed1 in mph and temp0 in deg F
' Then WindChill_C = (WindChill -32)/1.8
'SigmaPhi &
'SigmaTheta-stability at level 1 only, nighttime shortwave down measurement <6 W/m2
'
'Modify datalogger program at TA-06 to:
'a. Estimate hourly snowfall for the Public tables every hour.
'   See attached for calculation.
'b. Output snowfall since midnight into Public table.
'c. Output daily snowfall into 24 hour file.
'd. Output midnight temperature into 24 hour file.

'Added snowfall estimation including Public table variables
'Public SnowDepth_in,Dist2Target, Snow(3),SnowDepth_in_Avg
'Dim i, Snow_15min(8)
'Dim SmoothSnow(6)
'Dim SnowDiff(4)
'Public LastHrPrecip,AirT_HrAvg,SnowHr_in, SnowToday_in
'Public SnowTrace As String
'===========================================================================
'
'
'
'
'Version 7: 07312017_GTStanton, Updated PIR2(LWUP)Eppley Constant to 4.17 from 3.75,
' installed SN28135F3 removed SN281125F3.
'Version 6:  07032017_GTStanton, Adjusting Distance to Ground (Ref. Surface Offset)
' for SR50; 78.09.
'Version 6:  GTStanton, Adjusting Distance to Ground (Reference Surface Offset)
' for SR50; 77.73.
'Version 6:  GTStanton, Adjusting Distance to Ground (Reference Surface Offset) for
' SR50; 77.87.
'Version 6: Jacob Davis, CSI; Changed SR50 code to use SDI12 instead of pulse train out.
''
' Version 5;  updated SR50 Snow Sensor offset to 80.355 from 80.40 to
' re-zero distance to ground surface (GTS).
''
'Version: 4_1 09-08-2016 --GTStanton, LANL Met Tech.
'Confirmed the change of the BrHalf Measurement settings to False from True for wind
' directions & Air Temps this has corrected
'the deviations in wind direction readings we have seen since implementing
'the CR3000 logger replaceing the CR7 Loggers.  Went Through and confirmed BrHalf Meas
'for Air Temp & Wind Directions are now FALSE.
'Made further refinement adjustment to the SR50 Snow Sensor for zeroing and
't-shooting, after sensor failure.
'The additional varistors installed at this site for lightning protection seem
'to affect the dual swing excitation/scaling of the BRHalf operation.
'
'Version: 4  07-14-2016  --GTStanton, LANL
'Corrected error in 15Min Data Table for L-4 Wind Direction Averaging; was directed
' to L-4 Wind Speed incorrectedly
'Also identified that the BrHalf Measurement setting of True instead of False
'may be introducing error into the Wind Direction Measurement Averages,
'as a result of the Negative Voltage Excitation Swing.
' I am changing one of the Wind Direction & One of the Air Temp Settings
' to FALSE to see if it generates
'the averages more correctly to meld with our historical program data sets.
'
'
'Still Version 3 for deployment; updated 07072016 Eppley Sensor constants to new
' hardware as installed.
' LWUP/PIR2 was previously 3.66 is now 3.75
' LWDN/PIR1 was previously 3.37 is now 3.37
' SWDN/PSP1 was previously 8.62 is now 8.62
' SWUP/PSP2 was previously 9.39 is now 7.90
'----Nothing Further At this time---- GTStanton
'
'Version:  3  August 20, 2015  GTStanton
'Updated Solar Sensor Constants/Multipliers
'Adjusted Vertical Wind Multiplier for the Cosine Measurement Effect 1.25/0.0225
'Corrected Wm2 multiplier from 1E5 to 1E6
'
'Version: 2 August 18, 2015 - Jacob Davis, CSI
'  Added snow depth measurement

'Version: 2 August 17, 2015 - Jacob Davis, CSI
'    Wholesale renaming of solar radiation variables.
'     As they were called      	New Label       	Indicates
'             EppPSP1	                 SWDN	         Short Wave Down/Incoming
'             EppPSP2	                 SWUP	         Short Wave Up/Outgoing/Return
'             PIR1	                   LWDN	         Long Wave Down/Incoming
'             PIR2	                   LWUP	         Long Wave Up/Outgoing/Return
'Added RH to 24 hour table as well
'
